<title>JAPAN: Japan May long-term prime seen at 3.1 pct--bankers.</title>
<headline>Japan May long-term prime seen at 3.1 pct--bankers.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's long-term prime lending rate for May is likely to be set at 3.1 percent, up 0.6 percentage point from 2.5 percent in April, bankers said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The new rate would be the highest level since August 1996, when it was 3.3 percent.</p>
<p>The Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd (IBJ) said it would announce its prime lending rate for May at 6.00 p.m. (0900 GMT) on Monday.</p>
<p>The prime rate, which is applied to loans of one year and longer to Japanese long-term credit banks' most creditworthy clients, is reviewed every month, reflecting market trends.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8570</p>
